{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae","id":1564416,"title":"Protection against Fae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-09-29T05:49:40-07:00","id":1564416,"title":"Protection against Fae","content":"I\u2019ve tried looking up various sourcebooks, but either not seeing the info i\u2019m looking for or not looking at correct books.<br /> can anyone help me find what vampires have available to protect Against Fae?<br /> <br /> even if you just put the source material and page number\u2026<br /> <br /> got a few suggestions about salt, but was told thats from a different system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28559-malachy","name":"Malachy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28559_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-29T08:00:29-07:00","id":1564418,"title":"","content":"To be honest I'm not sure I udnerstand the question, but I hope I can answer<br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness vampires do not have a wide array of specialized anti-Fae gear because the two factions rarely interact.<br /> However, when a conflict does occur, vampires &quot;rely&quot; on a mix of mortal Banality, physical Disciplines, and Cold Iron.<br /> <br /> In WoD the Ultimate Anti-Fae Weapon is Cold Iron<br /> Pure, hand-forged iron completely bypasses all Faerie magical defenses and inflicts aggravated damage on Changelings.<br /> But &quot;Cold Iron&quot; is a bit murky, many say 'hand forged&quot;, - It must be created through traditional, low-tech methods (like a charcoal fire and manual hammering) rather than modern blast furnaces. In some interpretations, it includes meteoric iron that hasn't been heated by human agency - other sources say true cold iron must never be heated by human hands.<br /> <br /> Fae magic (Chimerical realities and Glamour) can easily trick a vampire's mind, but high-level sensory Disciplines can defend against them.<br /> Auspex Level 2 (Aura Perception) is a vampire's primary defensive tool to identify a Fae creature. It reveals the vibrant, ever-shifting nature of a Changeling's aura compared to the pale, stagnant aura of a mortal or the dead aura of a vampire.<br /> Mytherceria Level 1 (Folderol) allows a vampire to immediately detect any active Fae illusions or lies.<br /> (Vampire: The Masquerade 20th Anniversary Edition, p. 135 (Auspex rules) and Lore of the Bloodlines, p. 116 (Mytherceria rules).)<br /> <i>Chimerstry</i> illusion also &quot;real&quot; to the Changleings and the Fae - and lethal sometimes <br /> <br /> Because Changelings still possess physical, living bodies, they are vulnerable to a vampire's mental attacks, giving Kindred a major defensive edge if they strike first.\u200b\u200b<br /> Vampires can use <b>Dominate</b> or <b>Presence</b> to completely override a Fae's mind or force them to flee<br /> However, because Fae possess alien minds, a vampire must usually spend <b>1 Willpower point</b> to successfully initiate mind-control disciplines against them. (This specific crossover ruling is detailed in <i><b>World of Darkness: Outcasts</b></i> (A Companion for Changeling, Werewolf, and Vampire) and reaffirmed in the <i>Storyteller Companion</i> crossover addendums.)\u200b<br /> <br /> The greatest passive protection a vampire has is simply existing. Vampires are creatures of stasis, death, and routine. In the World of Darkness, they are walking, sentient anchors of Banality.<br /> Prolonged exposure to a vampire actively chokes out a Changeling\u2019s Glamour, triggering the &quot;Undoings&quot; or forcing them into &quot;Bedlam&quot; (madness). Fae will actively avoid vampires because standing near one feels like suffocating. (Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Chapter One (The Nature of Banality). )<br /> Tho Malkavians, Maeghar and Kisayd a bit exception... sometimes.... a bit complicated<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy does feature specialized Wards and Warding Circles designed specifically to block and punish the Fae.<br /> Ward Versus Fae (Level 3 or 4 Ritual) This ritual allows a thaumaturge to enchant an object, space, or threshold (like a window, doorway, or weapon) to act as a lethal barrier against Fae entities (Detailed explicitly in Blood Magic: Secrets of Thaumaturgy, p. 95. Depending on the edition or specific printing, it is sometimes categorized as a Level 3 or Level 4 ritual)<br /> While a basic <i>Ward</i> protects a single discrete object or surface (like a doorknob), a <i>Warding Circle</i> secures an entire fixed geographic area\u200b - Warding Circle Versus Fae (Level 4 or 5 Ritual) (Appears in the compiled list of specialized circles in Vampire: The Masquerade 20th Anniversary Edition (V20), pp. 234\u2013235)<br /> <br /> If your Storyteller allows older Revised/Second edition paths, there is an entire primary path of Tremere magic dedicated to security called the Path of Warding<br /> At lower levels, it alerts the caster if a supernatural entity bypasses a boundary. At higher levels, it physically locks down space or inflicts variable damage based on how many successes the caster rolled. (Originally featured in early Sabbat and Tremere player handbooks.)<br /> <br /> I have foggy memories about Akhu - Settie Sorcery have something similar protection, but not sure about that one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-29T12:19:52-07:00","id":1564423,"title":"","content":"Wow awesome response - thank you.<br /> I was hoping for something like protection from glamour but will read over your answer. Cold Iron wasn\u2019t high on my list as carrying such a weapon may lead to hostilities\u2026.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28559-malachy","name":"Malachy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28559_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-29T12:27:23-07:00","id":1564424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malachy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae#post1564416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve tried looking up various sourcebooks, but either not seeing the info i\u2019m looking for or not looking at correct books.<br /> can anyone help me find what vampires have available to protect Against Fae?<br /> <br /> even if you just put the source material and page number\u2026<br /> <br /> got a few suggestions about salt, but was told thats from a different system.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Nothing. Period.</b><br /> <br /> Surmising what Shadeprowler said and contextualizing:<br /> <br /> <i>As a rule of thumb vampires don't know shit about the Fae and have absolutely nothing to use against them <u><b>specifically</b></u></i>. You can use the Occultism Knowledge to remember some folk practices and the likelihood of them working, but is a wild guess at best.<br /> <br /> That's your main answer. <b><u>As a vampire you're not prepared to deal with them, full stop</u></b>, unless you specifically have <i><b>Lore (Fae) </b></i>or similar as an Ability.<br /> <br /> IF you have those, then it <i>depends on how your ST runs Fae in Vampire</i>. You'll still not have any tool designed to deal with them, but that will say what works in general, which is great info in itself.<br /> <br /> Cold Iron is a reasonable guess in English speaking countries, but there's no fixed definition of what's Cold Iron. It's not just that the ST has to decide, but the characters themselves would be aware of the ambiguity rather than the answer going only with Occult.<br /> <br /> You're a Player or ST? What reference is being used for Fae in the game? How much is it expected to follow other gamelines?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-09T00:58:21-07:00","id":1564632,"title":"","content":"I would allow a character to develop Ward Against Fae or similar, like the other warding rituals, but I don't think there's even been one published formally (I could be wrong, though). Kiasyd might have some ideas about handling fae, but even then...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-10T01:37:54-07:00","id":1564660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564632#post1564632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would allow a character to develop Ward Against Fae or similar, like the other warding rituals, but I don't think there's even been one published formally (I could be wrong, though). Kiasyd might have some ideas about handling fae, but even then...</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but that's not available yet. A character that starts to deal with them can do a lot more by developing stuff, but until then?<br /> <br /> And it's interesting that they were do avoidant of Changeling at the time, even the Bloodline that deals with Fae have no published resource against Fae. How childish it can be?<br /> <br /> Ravnos do are overpowered against Fae if you use all published rules, but those are very bad rules. And then they're Fae hunters because reasons.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I think if the ST wants, giving the Kyasid knowledge and methods to deal with the Fae would be more than fitting. And would cost a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-10T10:00:58-07:00","id":1564667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malachy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564423#post1564423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow awesome response - thank you.<br /> I was hoping for something like protection from glamour but will read over your answer. Cold Iron wasn\u2019t high on my list as carrying such a weapon may lead to hostilities\u2026.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cold Iron is (allegedly) the only thing that can permanently slay a Fae, as it (allegedly) destroys their very spirit.<br /> <br /> I said 'allegedly', because it's also possible that cold iron purifies them of Banality and restores their status as true fae.<br /> <br /> Depends on which version of the lore your ST decides to go with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 10-10-2026, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-10T23:07:11-07:00","id":1564680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564667#post1564667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cold Iron is (allegedly) the only thing that can permanently slay a Fae, as it (allegedly) destroys their very spirit.<br /> <br /> I said 'allegedly', because it's also possible that cold iron purifies them of Banality and restores their status as true fae.<br /> <br /> Depends on which version of the lore your ST decides to go with.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they go with Changeling at all.<br /> <br /> Changeling is the single most ignored gameline in WoD to run splats in other lines. I've seen way more games of Vampire or Werewolf that make up shit without getting near Changeling than games that even tried to bring anything at all of its lore or rules.<br /> <br /> There are many posters here that have been STing WoD since the 90's or 2000's, know most books by heart, and still know almost nothing about Changeling, at all, not even what you learn reading the Introduction.<br /> <br /> So I'm serious when I say to not put too much stock on any official lore: the chances of backfiring because your ST simply does things their own way are considerably higher than average, and then <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> detailed answer, as good as it is, becomes meaningless.<br /> <br /> At most Cold Iron is a reasonable guess because it is a traditional Bane for British islands style fairies, but that's it and you have the whole problem of defining what it even is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-11T02:46:31-07:00","id":1564685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564680#post1564680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At most Cold Iron is a reasonable guess because it is a traditional Bane for British islands style fairies, but that's it and you have the whole problem of defining what it even is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other traditional banes I've researched in the past include such actions as<br /> <br /> <i>Wearing your clothes inside out.</i> This apparently confuses the fey and acts as a ward against their magic.<br /> <br /> <i>Hanging your shoes above the threshold of your property line.</i> I believe this is supposed to create a protective barrier the fey can not cross.<br /> <br /> <i>NEVER accept any gifts of food or drink they offer you.</i> Doing so contractually obligates you to serve the fey for a period of no shorter than a year and a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-11T04:36:37-07:00","id":1564686,"title":"","content":"These are less reliable as pop culture references, but sure are there. Throwing salt over your shoulder also wards off the fey, and most things that work against ghosts or demons may work against them.<br /> <br /> If you expand the concept beyond UK Fae, then things can go wild. Horseshoes over the door, an Alraune doll made with mandrake, wearing monster masks at certain times of the day and/or year.<br /> <br /> Hire someone to dress like you and perform a ritual imitation so the fairy will follow them and give up when they find out the mistake. Lots of things involving iron nails.<br /> <br /> One thing to worry depending on the ST is that there are many legends of vampiric beings that are fey, not undead. Actually the majority around the world. So you can have Fae that are competition for resources and capable at passing as Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-11T15:23:44-07:00","id":1564694,"title":"","content":"Just as an aside, it\u2019s worth noting that the Kiasyd bloodline from the Sabbat books is basically a fae-touched Kindred. The Lhiannan bloodline from Dark Ages may have some fae influence as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-11T18:01:11-07:00","id":1564697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564694#post1564694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as an aside, it\u2019s worth noting that the Kiasyd bloodline from the Sabbat books is basically a fae-touched Kindred. The Lhiannan bloodline from Dark Ages may have some fae influence as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Already commented.<br /> <br /> The problem is that even they have no published resources against Fae. No ritual, no special Discipline, no items or recorded lore. It is implied the Kiasyd know what to do and are a regular threat to local fey, but never went further than that, and Mytherceria is useless in this regard.<br /> <br /> Lhiannan are more spirit oriented, do depend a lot on your interpretation of the Fae. They're also more 'Pictish shamanic warriors', so their thing is all about knowing their area and having terrain advantage in battle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-12T08:11:15-07:00","id":1564702,"title":"","content":"I just remembered, and mind you that this relevance may vary depending on how you want to go about it, but the Kuei Jin are considered to be a serious threat to the Hsien (asian Changelings).<br /> <br /> The reason for this being that the Hsien's body is entirely composed of chi, which the Kuei Jin feed on to sustain themselves. Meaning that the Kuei Jin are natural predators of the Hsien.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-12T13:12:54-07:00","id":1564709,"title":"","content":"The Hsien are more like the Sebettu/Fallen of Demon:The Fallen<br /> Not to mention the Shinma have no connection to the Dreaming, Banality does not affect them and neither have any problem with Cold Iron; they cloak themselves in a mortal body, are able to assume mortal bodies... but thats it<br /> <b>Yugen</b> is addictive to the Kuei-jin and their relationship is sour thanks to whats happened after the Dragon River War at the begining of the Fourth Age<br /> Actually hunting a &quot;Little God&quot; is highly frowned upon and considered a dangerous taboo within mainstream Kuei-jin society - also carries massive social and spiritual consequences<br /> Hunting down and cannibalizing true celestial bureaucrats and minor deities\u2014even exiled ones like the Hsien\u2014is seen as a massive step backward into corruption in every Dharma<br /> ...not to mention the Hsien might be trapped in mortal bodies, but they are still ancient elemental spirits/celestial bureaucrats capable of wielding incredibly potent <b>Wu Tan</b> magic. A Kuei-jin attempting to hunt even a lesser Shinma risks facing the collective wrath of an entire Hsien Court, who hold a deep, thousands-of-years-old grudge against the Hungry Dead for ruining the Fourth Age already...<br /> And news spread. In the Middle Kingdom a Kuei-Jin Court co-exist with the Hsien Court, the Sprit Courts of the Yang World, potnetially a local necropolis of the Yin World, be either the Court of the Dark Kingdom of Jade or locals who resist the Jade Emperor and even the Hengeyokai local beats court, with emsiasaries and ambassadors all around<br /> Happens of course, especially among the young Runing Monkeys, accidentally usually, but the fallout usually a headache for everyone<br /> <br /> So natural predators...?<br /> No, not really<br /> <br /> The 1st edition ST guide mentions the Shadow Court has secret, high-placed allies within the Sabbat, specifically referencing the Kiasyd and that Unseelie Changelings occasionally make pacts with Kiasyd scholars to trade forbidden magical secrets for protection or political leverage against the Seelie Courts<br /> The enigmatic, 6th-generation Kiasyd known only as <b>The Arcadian from </b>Lore of the Bloodlines and the Changeling Storytellers Guide is canonized as having deep knowledge regarding the inner workings of both the Fae and Kindred politics. The historical origins of the bloodline also link their creation to specific Noble Houses of the Fae (with rumors pointing to <b>House Fiona</b> or <b>House Eshu</b> blood being used in the alchemical experiments that made them)<br /> Libellus Sanguinis 1: Masters of the State mentions Kiasyd sometimes acted as rare, uneasy neutral envoys between Lasombra-controlled mortal courts and the local Fae Freeholds. Their impeccably formal manners and adherence to strict protocols allowed them to navigate the rigid etiquette of Changeling Courts without instantly triggering conflict.<br /> And the Book of Lost Dreams provides the explicit system rules for how a Kiasyd interacts with a Changeling Court.\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 10-12-2026, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-12T15:35:24-07:00","id":1564711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564709#post1564709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And news spread. In the Middle Kingdom a Kuei-Jin Court co-exist with the Hsien Court, the Sprit Courts of the Yang World, potnetially a local necropolis of the Yin World, be either the Court of the Dark Kingdom of Jade or locals who resist the Jade Emperor and even the Hengeyokai local beats court, with emsiasaries and ambassadors all around<br /> Happens of course, especially among the young Runing Monkeys, accidentally usually, but the fallout usually a headache for everyone<br /> <br /> So natural predators...?<br /> No, not really<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>C20 does mention that the Hsien make for tempting targets of those who feed on Chi, and that if they are consumed in this way, it utterly destroys them.<br /> <br /> I coulda sworn I read a passage that specifically mentioned them being hunted down by the Kuei Jin, but I'm having trouble locating it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T12:08:11-07:00","id":1564726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564711#post1564711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> C20 does mention that the Hsien make for tempting targets of those who feed on Chi, and that if they are consumed in this way, it utterly destroys them.<br /> <br /> I coulda sworn I read a passage that specifically mentioned them being hunted down by the Kuei Jin, but I'm having trouble locating it now.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like how Werewolves can sometimes get a small extra benefit and a lot of pleasure from eating human meat, but it is actually a taboo and fast way to screw yourself.<br /> <br /> Or like Diablerie in Vampire, a source of power and a fast way to make enemies and become a dangerous addict because no one likes to be around a proven predator and murderer.<br /> <br /> Hsien are tasty for consumers of Chi. They're also a problem that should be avoided in this regard. Eating one will give the Kuei-Jin extra juice and a ton of enemies all over the place.<br /> <br /> And as Shadeprowler said, they're not Fae. Like at all. Why they're part of the Changeling line is a mystery precisely because it makes no sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T14:22:47-07:00","id":1564729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564726#post1564726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And as Shadeprowler said, they're not Fae. Like at all. Why they're part of the Changeling line is a mystery precisely because it makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>C20 described it as the people of Asia <i>&quot;Far from the courts of the Kithain, far from the Dreaming and the chimerical wonders they devote themselves to, mortals dream other dreams. They dream not of knights and dukes, of courtly love and chivalrous battle, but of shapeshifting raccoon dogs, of playful cats who know more than they let on, of monkey kings who topple even the pillars of heaven. They dream of the small gods of the 10,000 things - but those small gods dream only of walking the path between Heaven and Earth once more&quot;</i><br /> <br /> So, yeah, they basically said that Asian mythology was make believe, and thus they were close enough to be lumped in with Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T15:49:32-07:00","id":1564732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564726#post1564726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as Shadeprowler said, they're not Fae. Like at all. Why they're part of the Changeling line is a mystery precisely because it makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're &quot;changelings&quot; in the sense that they're born as normal children, just with their soul swapped out for that of an eldritch supernatural being that's trapped in an un-ending cycle of reincarnation. But they're not (proper noun) Changelings in the manner of Changeling: the Dreaming, so they don't have ties to the Dreaming or power over dreams.<br /> <br /> It's basically just like how the Wan Kuei are &quot;vampires&quot; that feed on blood or life energy, but they're not (proper noun) Vampires like you see in Vampire: The Masquerade. They're a type of vampire, but they're not Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T19:34:46-07:00","id":1564737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564729#post1564729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">C20 described it as the people of Asia <i>&quot;Far from the courts of the Kithain, far from the Dreaming and the chimerical wonders they devote themselves to, mortals dream other dreams. They dream not of knights and dukes, of courtly love and chivalrous battle, but of shapeshifting raccoon dogs, of playful cats who know more than they let on, of monkey kings who topple even the pillars of heaven. They dream of the small gods of the 10,000 things - but those small gods dream only of walking the path between Heaven and Earth once more&quot;</i><br /> <br /> So, yeah, they basically said that Asian mythology was make believe, and thus they were close enough to be lumped in with Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's less an affirmation and more just purple prose. It's a very poetic way of saying &quot;we'll talk about those things here and use this book's vernacular, precision be damned&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or, in other words, C20 talks about them in the terms of dreams because C20 talks in terms of dreams, period. Think of it as the Hsien being described in-game in a treatise about Gallain by some Kithain scholar. It's not a neutral book, much less culturally conscious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564732#post1564732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're &quot;changelings&quot; in the sense that they're born as normal children, just with their soul swapped out for that of an eldritch supernatural being that's trapped in an un-ending cycle of reincarnation. But they're not (proper noun) Changelings in the manner of Changeling: the Dreaming, so they don't have ties to the Dreaming or power over dreams.<br /> <br /> It's basically just like how the Wan Kuei are &quot;vampires&quot; that feed on blood or life energy, but they're not (proper noun) Vampires like you see in Vampire: The Masquerade. They're a type of vampire, but they're not Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>True-ish, but as Shadeprowler I think under the current state of WoD they're more akin to the Fallen than the Fae. It's just that they got written way before.<br /> <br /> Many themes and assumptions on how Demon works arised first in the Hsien. They're the first prototype, and Demon even has mechanics here and there that look like improvements for the Hsien in a new edition rather than a purely new splat.<br /> <br /> And we have the added problem that the Little Gods actually depart from Changeling in theme and mood way more than any other Far East splat does, and then continues to mechanics, at most having a passing resemblance rather than any similarity in rules, fluff or metaphysics of what's happening.<br /> <br /> If I someday finish my revamp of Demon, I'll definitely move the Hsien there. And follow the precedents of C20 supplements to expand on actual Asian Fae in some other way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-13T23:35:39-07:00","id":1564741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564737#post1564737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If I someday finish my revamp of Demon, I'll definitely move the Hsien there. And follow the precedents of C20 supplements to expand on actual Asian Fae in some other way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would a Yaoguai be more appropriate take on them? From my understanding of the mythology, a Yaoguai is an animal, plant, object, or even a terrain feature that <i>'awakened to sentience'</i> after existing for an extended period of time (often a century or more).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-14T13:12:34-07:00","id":1564750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564741#post1564741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Yaoguai be more appropriate take on them? From my understanding of the mythology, a Yaoguai is an animal, plant, object, or even a terrain feature that <i>'awakened to sentience'</i> after existing for an extended period of time (often a century or more).</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely.<br /> <br /> Yaoguai/Youkai (is the same word and meaning) are actually more diverse than &quot;just&quot; those, but so are fairies.<br /> <br /> Overall, legends of Yaoguai would be better inspiration for East Asian Fae, and the word a better Chinese term for them. Which is fitting because Chinese is to them similar to Latin in Europe.<br /> <br /> Now, would be a 1:1 equivalent? No, but again so it is with Fae. Not everything called a Yaoguai would be a Changeling and vice-versa, but the overall shape remains.<br /> <br /> I'd say the &quot;awakened&quot; things would probably be a Kith-equivalent or a Gallain similar to the Inanimae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-14T15:36:37-07:00","id":1564753,"title":"","content":"The key difference between Changelings (both types) and Demons is that Changelings are born into what they are. Even as babies they've already got the soul of a much older, eldritch being within them. With Demons however, they end up fusing with the body of a normal human, typically one who is much older and has already experienced a childhood, years as a teenager and even frequently been an (normal) adult for some time.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, the process of how Hsien are born is why White Wolf considered them to be a type of changeling and put them in with Changeling: the Dreaming. Likewise they felt that Wan Kuei, as blood drinkers, were better classified as a type of vampire and added them to Vampire the Masquerade, rather than a type of Risen and linked them with Wraith: The Oblivion.<br /> <br /> I think there are definitely strong arguments as to why Wan Kuei might be better classified as something besides Vampires, and Hsien aren't really Changelings at all, that was just White Wolf's logic as to why those groups were put in with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-14T16:52:50-07:00","id":1564755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564753#post1564753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Demons however, they end up fusing with the body of a normal human, typically one who is much older and has already experienced a childhood, years as a teenager and even frequently been an (normal) adult for some time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, is that not what the Changelings are?<br /> <br /> A fae spirit that attaches itself to (and merges with) a human soul? Then when that physical body dies, they move on to another?<br /> <br /> Also, being Changelings is not their default state. They were True Fae who adopted the Changeling Way as a means of protecting themselves from Banality; and even then, most of the Sidhe rejected the idea entirely and chose to flee to Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-15T13:01:06-07:00","id":1564764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564755#post1564755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, is that not what the Changelings are?<br /> <br /> A fae spirit that attaches itself to (and merges with) a human soul? Then when that physical body dies, they move on to another?<br /> <br /> Also, being Changelings is not their default state. They were True Fae who adopted the Changeling Way as a means of protecting themselves from Banality; and even then, most of the Sidhe rejected the idea entirely and chose to flee to Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that the Fae soul (and god-soul for Hsien) attach itself to the baby while it's still in the womb. So The Changeling and Hsien never really grow up normal, they're supernatural even as children. Meanwhile with other splats like Demons, or Mummies typically the supernatural essence attaches itself to someone who's already an adult and that has gone through a decade or two of being a normal, mundane individual and now has supernatural power. Even mages usually don't have their Avatar awaken until later in life.<br /> <br /> For the changelings (Hsien and Changelings) the fact that they were already born and interacting with the supernatural even in early childhood is the defining point of the splat. This goes back to the folklore idea of &quot;changelings&quot; which is that faeries or other supernatural beings swapped out a normal baby for one of their supernatural babies. So from White Wolf's perspective, this is what made Hsien a type of changeling, even though they don't interact with the Dreaming. The way they are born and experience the world starting from the earliest days of childhood puts them in a similar storyline as Changelings from Changeling the Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-15-2026, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-15T14:56:11-07:00","id":1564765,"title":"","content":"I personally like the fact that European Kithain go through three stages in their lifecycle (Childling, Wilder and Grump). I think the fact that changelings are supernatural beings even in childhood distinguishes them from most other supernaturals (even Garou, who typically go through the First Change in adolescence).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-15T15:06:18-07:00","id":1564767,"title":"","content":"<b>*sigh~* damn it, editing flag...</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564764#post1564764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difference is that the Fae soul (and god-soul for Hsien) attach itself to the baby while it's still in the womb. So The Changeling and Hsien never really grow up normal, they're supernatural even as children. Meanwhile with other splats like Demons, or Mummies typically the supernatural essence attaches itself to someone who's already an adult and that has gone through a decade or two of being a normal, mundane individual and now has supernatural power. Even mages usually don't have their Avatar awaken until later in life.<br /> <br /> For the changelings (Hsien and Changelings) the fact that they were already born and interacting with the supernatural even in early childhood is the defining point of the splat. This goes back to the folklore idea of &quot;changelings&quot; which is that faeries or other supernatural beings swapped out a normal baby for one of their supernatural babies. So from White Wolf's perspective, this is what made Hsien a type of changeling, even though they don't interact with the Dreaming. The way they are born and experience the world starting from the earliest days of childhood puts them in a similar storyline as Changelings from Changeling the Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure they specifically have to be unborn children for the merger to happen?<br /> <br /> At least in the case of Arcadian Sidhe, it makes it explicitly clear that they just grabbed whatever bodies happened to be within arm's reach and booted the human's soul out.<br /> <br /> Also, the Changeling's Seeming age fluctuates depending on their perception of the world, and can spontaneously shift between any stage of Childling, Wilder or Grump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-15T22:43:10-07:00","id":1564775,"title":"","content":"Guess what , forum ate my post... I will delete the original<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564764#post1564764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difference is that the Fae soul (and god-soul for Hsien) attach itself to the baby while it's still in the womb. So The Changeling and Hsien never really grow up normal, they're supernatural even as children. Meanwhile with other splats like Demons, or Mummies typically the supernatural essence attaches itself to someone who's already an adult and that has gone through a decade or two of being a normal, mundane individual and now has supernatural power. Even mages usually don't have their Avatar awaken until later in life.<br /> <br /> For the changelings (Hsien and Changelings) the fact that they were already born and interacting with the supernatural even in early childhood is the defining point of the splat. This goes back to the folklore idea of &quot;changelings&quot; which is that faeries or other supernatural beings swapped out a normal baby for one of their supernatural babies. So from White Wolf's perspective, this is what made Hsien a type of changeling, even though they don't interact with the Dreaming. The way they are born and experience the world starting from the earliest days of childhood puts them in a similar storyline as Changelings from Changeling the Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well not that much<br /> When a Hsien spirit undergoes <b>Kun Shou</b> (the process of taking over a mortal vessel whose original soul has just departed at the brink of death), the age of the body dictates their classification<br /> The Hsien-tsu are usually infants of children, mostly <b>Hirayanu</b> (the animal-associated commoners, like the Tanuki or Nyan) are Hsien-tsu. They grow up with human families, though they inherently know what they are. They tend to be more lighthearted<br /> While the Hsien-jin - anyone are 15+ - are mostly Mostly <b>Kamuii</b> (the noble elemental spirits, like the Fu Hsi or Chu Jung). They instantly animate a fully grown adult who was dying. Because it would be too jarring for the human's family to witness a sudden, radical personality shift, Hsien-jin typically sever all ties with the host's former life immediately. They are much more serious and driv<br /> <br /> For an adult <i>hotei</i>, there is no gestation. The celestial spirit swoops into a dying body, heals it enough to function, and hits the ground running with its own divine agenda.<br /> For the Hsien there are no &quot;merge&quot; or born into something like the Changeling - they are literally like the Sebettu except when they bit the daust they don't have to seek out a new host asap fearing the Abyss. The celestial spirit leaves the broken physical vessel and immediately travels to the Spirit World (the Middle Umbra / Yang Realm). Once in the spirit realm, the Hsien is brought before the divine magistrates to face judgment. They are strictly evaluated on how well they fulfilled their spiritual duties and balanced their elemental nature while on Earth . Most Hsien are sent right back to the mortal world to serve again. However, this cycle comes with a heavy price: they are forced into a new host body, and they lose a large portion of their memories from their past life. Piecing together who they used to be becomes a major struggle in their next incarnation.<br /> <br /> So they are like the Sebettu with a healthy dose of Amenti streak<br /> There is technically no similarities except this host body thing between them and the Changelings and even needing/having a body is basically different\u200b\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-15T22:45:44-07:00","id":1564776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564753#post1564753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The key difference between Changelings (both types) and Demons is that Changelings are born into what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not actually true, especially because you're retroactively attributing to White Wolf an intention based on distinctions that would only exist several years later.<br /> <br /> Changeling came 7 years before Demon, in a time when their publishing schedule and development pace was insane, it could easily have been 21 years at Paradox pace. It came mid to early 2nd Edition and Demon came near the end of Revised.<br /> <br /> When the Hsien were created Demon didn't exist in any relevant form as a future product. It isn't like the Kuei-Jin who were thought as a counterpart to an established line.<br /> <br /> KotE was designed as a foil to VtM. They're not treated as Kindred because of having Kindred like traits, they have Kindred like traits because that was the point of their design. White Wolf had a theme for the Year and KotE was the result, the end, however good or bad that is.<br /> <br /> Now, could they change association to Wraith, instead? Yes. Could they treat as a standalone line? Also yes. They did with Mummy, that's actually one of the oldest splats but as another VtM expansion.<br /> <br /> But the question isn't what they can. It's where it brings more benefits. Keeping within a line means facilitating communication, enforcing a minimum compatibility and keeping them as a same set. KotE is a VtM product not because it is metaphysically close to Kindred, its because they're meant to interact with VtM and enforce the division of territory between the two groups.<br /> <br /> And that's also the reason Hengeyoukai stayed a staple while KotE, being far more popular, got ignored, sidestepped, and overall became a big problem for the publishers. Not because it was a bad game, but because it was a problematic part of VtM.<br /> <br /> Moving it to Wraith would improve things? Not really as they didn't had much reason to interact with Wraith at this level, either. If KotE is ever to become a thing again (which I hope it does), it should be as its own line.<br /> <br /> Now, Changeling. First things first, the Sidhe do exactly this very thing, possessing an adult body and sending the soul somewhere else. They have zero need to be children first.<br /> <br /> Even the others don't start life as supernatural beings, that's simply not true, at least no more than any Changing Breed. They're not special until their Chrysalis, and that's as likely to happen after 13 than before.<br /> <br /> It is true that both Changelings and Hsien have in common the themes of fused souls born this way that tend to come into their powers at childhood, but that's a secondary design choice made because the intention to have them related predates any decision on who they are.<br /> <br /> It's also true that there are exceptions among Changelings and going Changeling style is an option in Demon, especially today.<br /> <br /> What I think is that the Hsien have little to nothing to contribute in Changeling. They don't interact meaningfully with the Kithain. They don't deal with similar stuff. Their energy sources are thematically closer to Faith than Glamour. A crossover between the two splats has no common ground to work with, which is ok but also means it's just any crossover.<br /> <br /> Have they something to contribute as standalone? Maybe, but I think a participation in Demon actually does benefit both lines. They share metaphysical roles and possibly some history. They have reason to have strong opinions on each other. To feel kinship or hate. They dispute the same resource and have a similar situation as exiles.<br /> <br /> Seriously, they have every reason to be canon to each other and establish interactions. To be a factor for the other splat. They're just not the same line because of a 7 year difference on when each was published.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-15T23:11:02-07:00","id":1564777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564765#post1564765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally like the fact that European Kithain go through three stages in their lifecycle (Childling, Wilder and Grump). I think the fact that changelings are supernatural beings even in childhood distinguishes them from most other supernaturals (even Garou, who typically go through the First Change in adolescence).</div> </div> </div> </div>So, a few corrections.<br /> <br /> 1. The Kithain are specifically British, and even then mostly Irish. The influence of other fairies from Europe is minimal and restricted to a few Kiths.<br /> <br /> Even the Eshu calls much more to old tales of African travelers to Europe before the 16th century, as those tales reached the Island, than actual legends from anywhere else.<br /> <br /> Changeling is the most geographically specific splat in WoD, and that's by design. The Kithain don't represent all forms of dreams or big universal archetypes, and the game is adamant that even small changes in cultural background metaphysically change the Fae that culture has links to.<br /> <br /> US White Changelings are Irish because that's where the mainstream White US culture took its fairies from. And that's ok.<br /> <br /> 2. They don't necessarily go through 3 stages, just to clarify. That's not uncommon, but plenty Kithain start as Wilder or already Grump and never go backwards. It's more common than a Changeling living to reach Grump from Childling.<br /> <br /> 3. Most supernaturals can start as children and many Changelings don't do so, the distinction isn't as strict as it seems. What's maybe more precise is that Changelings are the only splat socially prepared to deal with this. Demons are the second place, they can and do have child possessors without a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564767#post1564767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>*sigh~* damn it, editing flag...</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Try leaving the page and going back before the edit, helps. Isn't the ideal, but we won't get ideal here.<br /> <br /> So, for the Changeling Way it has to be unborn. The Changeling in fact makes no choice. They are sent into a reincarnation cycle and that's that.<br /> <br /> Regular possession, like the Arcadian Sidhe do, is distinct from the Changeling Way. Then sure, you grab whatever you want and the original soul is theoretically sent to Arcadia. But you do give up on this option for good when you do the Changeling Way. The benefit outside moral tranquility is reliability, since you don't have to seek a new body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-15T23:23:01-07:00","id":1564779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564776#post1564776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have they something to contribute as standalone? Maybe, but I think a participation in Demon actually does benefit both lines. They share metaphysical roles and possibly some history. They have reason to have strong opinions on each other. To feel kinship or hate. They dispute the same resource and have a similar situation as exiles.<br /> <br /> Seriously, they have every reason to be canon to each other and establish interactions. To be a factor for the other splat. They're just not the same line because of a 7 year difference on when each was published.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hsien were originally glorious, fully divine spirits living in the heavens. During the mythical <b>Age of Legends</b>, they messed up. They grew arrogant, neglected their duties, and mismanaged the mortal world. As punishment, the <b>August Personage of Jade</b> stripped them of their true divine forms. They were <b>exiled to Earth</b> (and learned to hide in human flesh (<i>hotei</i>) to survive).<br /> Basically they were Fallen before Fallen existed<br /> I even would go a mile and would say the Sebettu are just Hsien with &quot;extra punishment&quot; - purely headcanon of course, but there is an actual dark faction of the Hsien already who are suspiciusly like the Fallen all but name and Abyss (well depending how exactly you treat Yomi). The Sebettu might as well could be Hsien who sided with the Yama Kingsduring the War and became twisted, monstrous, parasitic entities that feed on dark Chi, torment, and misery. So insted exile they got a prison sentance. You don't even have to throw out the rich myth of WoD for it to work and wrote it off as illusion of grandeur... \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-15T23:34:39-07:00","id":1564781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564416-protection-against-fae?p=1564779#post1564779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Hsien were originally glorious, fully divine spirits living in the heavens. During the mythical <b>Age of Legends</b>, they messed up. They grew arrogant, neglected their duties, and mismanaged the mortal world. As punishment, the <b>August Personage of Jade</b> stripped them of their true divine forms. They were <b>exiled to Earth</b> (and learned to hide in human flesh (<i>hotei</i>) to survive).<br /> Basically they were Fallen before Fallen existed<br /> I even would go a mile and would say the Sebettu are just Hsien with &quot;extra punishment&quot; - purely headcanon of course, but there is an actual dark faction of the Hsien already who are suspiciusly like the Fallen all but name and Abyss (well depending how exactly you treat Yomi). The Sebettu might as well could be Hsien who sided with the Yama Kingsduring the War and became twisted, monstrous, parasitic entities that feed on dark Chi, torment, and misery. So insted exile they got a prison sentance. You don't even have to throw out the rich myth of WoD for it to work and wrote it off as illusion of grandeur...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd only change that they're the same class of beings, but got punished at different moments, for different crimes. I don't think assuming either lore as true over the other is the best approach, and that would subordinate Demon's lore to the Hsien.<br /> <br /> Are them &quot;divinities&quot; serving the same hierarchy before their fall? Maybe, maybe not. Did they knew each other in the past? Possibly, but both would find it hard to verify today.<br /> <br /> What we can say for sure: the Sebettu chose to go full rebellion in a very ancient war and got a prison sentence and excised from the hierarchy. The Hsien &quot;only&quot; neglected their duty during a possibly later period and got exiled but still tied to the hierarchy. That creates a category difference that doesn't make them completely distinct beings, but by their nature also means they can have quite different mechanics without immediate explanation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr